    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_2f72c707b6f8cd84728286d43aefaefa99de162e128ca7346097d069d0a95400",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Takeuchi's characterization converts arithmeticity of the lattice from a geometric label into an algebraic obstruction test on trace data: the trace-generated field must be a finite extension of the rationals, the traces must be integral, and the images required by the stated nonidentity embedding clause must remain bounded. A stronger, separately qualified embedding condition characterizes quaternion-algebra origin. The reformulation gains an intrinsic classification test and singles out the arithmetic Hecke parameters three, four, and six, but it does not explain their later spectral behavior.",
