    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_4d1b898652181320a891bb7639bf5bff8eb15917bda28fc8d027da8d1f6aa061",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The Poisson-versus-GOE heuristic is a scale-dependent surrogate, not a global classification: in the stated two-dimensional high-energy setting it models number variance only through an intermediate window, while nonuniversal, system-specific oscillations take over beyond the crossover. The scale-indexed representation gains a clean separation between locally universal correlation behavior and retained system-specific information, but loses any warrant to extrapolate random-matrix behavior to all spectral scales.",
      "parent_sources": [
