    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_5c3e5ffe6e5fbee19e10b4f56ccb46765a7207c70035a03e9a36cae762cfd937",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "A positive-dimensional family of trajectories sharing a period can affect long-range spectral fluctuations even when it occupies measure zero in phase space. For the stated closed two-dimensional setting, the two-dimensional fixed set of the time-periodic geodesic flow is the intermediate object linking coherent recurrence to a lower bound on averaged counting fluctuations and hence number variance. This gains a dynamical diagnostic for nonrigidity, but only a lower bound: it neither supplies the analytic trace mechanism nor automatically extends the theorem to billiards with boundary.",
